{"from": "passage:mk-01-01", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-01-01", "note": "Opening titles; Matthew 1:1 heads the genealogy of Jesus the Christ, Mark 1:1 the 'beginning of the Good News of Jesus Christ, the Son of God'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-04", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-03-01", "note": "John baptizing and preaching in the wilderness; Matthew 3:1-6 condenses the same ministry."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-05", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-03-05", "note": "Judeans and Jerusalemites going out to John and being baptized in the Jordan."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-06", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-03-04", "note": "John's camel-hair garment, leather belt, locusts and wild honey."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-09", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-03-13", "note": "Jesus comes from Galilee (Mark adds Nazareth) to be baptized by John in the Jordan."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-10", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-03-16", "note": "The Spirit descending like a dove as Jesus comes up from the water."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-11", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-03-17", "note": "The voice from the sky, 'You are my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-12", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-04-01", "note": "The Spirit leads/drives Jesus into the wilderness after the baptism."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-13", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-04-02", "note": "Partial: Mark's forty days with the wild animals; Matthew adds forty nights of fasting and the dialogued temptations."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-14", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-04-12", "note": "After John's arrest Jesus comes into Galilee."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-15", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-04-17", "note": "Jesus preaches that the kingdom is at hand and calls for repentance."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-16", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-04-18", "note": "Simon and Andrew called while casting a net into the sea."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-19", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-04-21", "note": "James and John called while mending nets in their father Zebedee's boat."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-20", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-04-22", "note": "They leave Zebedee in the boat with the hired servants and follow."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-29", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-08-14", "note": "Jesus enters Simon's house in Capernaum; Matthew names Peter's house."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-30", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-08-14", "note": "Simon's mother-in-law sick with a fever."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-31", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-08-15", "note": "He raises her, the fever leaves, and she serves them."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-32", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-08-16", "note": "At evening after sunset the sick and demon-possessed are brought to him."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-34", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-08-16", "note": "He heals many and casts out many demons."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-39", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-04-23", "note": "Preaching in the synagogues throughout Galilee."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-40", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-08-02", "note": "A leper kneels and asks to be made clean."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-41", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-08-03", "note": "Jesus touches the leper and the leprosy departs."}
{"from": "passage:mk-01-44", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-08-04", "note": "Show yourself to the priest and offer what Moses commanded."}
