{"from": "site:monastery-of-temptation", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-01-13-forty-days-tempted", "grade": "D", "note": "The 6th-century monastery above the cave 'traditionally said to be that where Jesus spent forty days and forty nights fasting' attests the commemorative tradition of the wilderness temptation, not the event (reception, grade D; it also commemorates Matthew's fasting, which Mark does not mention)."}
{"from": "text:josephus-war-1-pompey-sabbath", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-01-21-taught-capernaum-synagogue", "grade": "C", "note": "Josephus, War 1.145-147 (Whiston): at Pompey's siege the Jews abstained from work on the seventh days - Sabbath observance was a firm 1st-century institution. It attests the Sabbath setting of the synagogue visit, not the teaching event."}
